.TH EXIT 2
.SH NAME
exit \- terminate process
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "exit(status)"
.B "int status;"
.sp
.B "_exit(status)"
.B "int status;"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B exit
is the normal means of terminating a process.
.B exit
closes all the process'
files and notifies the parent process if it is executing a
.BR wait (2).
The
low-order 8 bits of
.I status
are available to the parent process.
.PP
This call can never return.
.PP
The C function
.B exit
may cause cleanup actions before the final `sys exit'.
The function
.B _exit
circumvents all cleanup.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
wait(2)
.SH ASSEMBLER
(exit = 1.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
R0 = status
sys exit
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 1
AX = status
int 0Xf1
.fi
.sp
